{"name":"December Solstice","hex":"#9dcee3","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"solstice","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["One of the two points in the ecliptic at which the sun is furthest from the celestial equator. This corresponds to one of two days in the year when the day is either longest or shortest."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/solstice"}],"entries":[{"title":"December solstice","blocks":[{"text":"The December solstice, also known as the southern solstice, is the solstice that occurs each December – typically on 21 December, but may vary by one day in either direction according to the Gregorian calendar. In the Northern Hemisphere, the December solstice is the winter solstice, whilst in the Southern Hemisphere it is the summer solstice. During the December solstice, the Sun is directly over the Tropic of Capricorn, located in the Southern Hemisphere."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4d/Earth-lighting-winter-solstice_EN.png/330px-Earth-lighting-winter-solstice_EN.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/December_solstice","wikidata":"Q5249063"},{"title":"December","blocks":[{"text":"December is the 12th and final month of the year in the Julian and Gregorian calendars. Its length is 31 days."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c8/12_December_-_Percent_of_global_area_at_temperature_records_-_Global_warming_-_NOAA.svg/330px-12_December_-_Percent_of_global_area_at_temperature_records_-_Global_warming_-_NOAA.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/December","wikidata":"Q126"},{"title":"Solstice","blocks":[{"text":"A solstice is the time when the Sun reaches its most northerly or southerly sun path relative to the celestial equator on the celestial sphere. Two solstices occur annually, around 20–22 June and 20–22 December. In many countries, the seasons of the year are defined by reference to the solstices and the equinoxes."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Solstice","wikidata":"Q123524"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6e/Les_Tr%C3%A8s_Riches_Heures_du_duc_de_Berry_d%C3%A9cembre.jpg/500px-Les_Tr%C3%A8s_Riches_Heures_du_duc_de_Berry_d%C3%A9cembre.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6e/Les_Tr%C3%A8s_Riches_Heures_du_duc_de_Berry_d%C3%A9cembre.jpg/500px-Les_Tr%C3%A8s_Riches_Heures_du_duc_de_Berry_d%C3%A9cembre.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"December, from the Très Riches Heures du duc de Berry","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALes_Tr%C3%A8s_Riches_Heures_du_duc_de_Berry_d%C3%A9cembre.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2e/Hans_Bol_-_Adriaen_Collaert_-_Emblemata_evangelica_-_Erfgoedfonds_Koning_Boudewijnstichting_-_Fonds_du_Patrimoine_Fondation_Roi_Baudouin_-_12.jpg/500px-Hans_Bol_-_Adriaen_Collaert_-_Emblemata_evangelica_-_Erfgoedfonds_Koning_Boudewijnstichting_-_Fonds_du_Patrimoine_Fondation_Roi_Baudouin_-_12.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2e/Hans_Bol_-_Adriaen_Collaert_-_Emblemata_evangelica_-_Erfgoedfonds_Koning_Boudewijnstichting_-_Fonds_du_Patrimoine_Fondation_Roi_Baudouin_-_12.jpg/1280px-Hans_Bol_-_Adriaen_Collaert_-_Emblemata_evangelica_-_Erfgoedfonds_Koning_Boudewijnstichting_-_Fonds_du_Patrimoine_Fondation_Roi_Baudouin_-_12.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2e/Hans_Bol_-_Adriaen_Collaert_-_Emblemata_evangelica_-_Erfgoedfonds_Koning_Boudewijnstichting_-_Fonds_du_Patrimoine_Fondation_Roi_Baudouin_-_12.jpg/500px-